              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 1.6
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "DRHhl",
              "name": "Reasons",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "gap": 22,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "yXVWr",
                  "name": "Google forces our hand",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 5,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "BLiBF",
                      "name": "Title",
                      "fill": "$text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Google forces our hand",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "HjBI0",
                      "name": "Body",
                      "fill": "$dim",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Deleting a parent in Google Tasks deletes its subtasks. If we promoted children locally we would diverge from the remote on every Google-backed task, and the next pull would resurrect or orphan them. Half the data cannot follow a rule we invent.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "AxdK6",
                  "name": "One rule, not two",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 5,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Wcuo7",
                      "name": "Title",
                      "fill": "$text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "One rule, not two",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Pm9Zh",
                      "name": "Body",
                      "fill": "$dim",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Local tasks could safely promote, but then delete would mean different things depending on where a task came from — invisible in the UI, since merged tabs deliberately hide provenance. A single rule is worth more than a marginally safer one.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "ogBRv",
                  "name": "Undo carries the safety",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 5,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "xh8Ia",
                      "name": "Title",
                      "fill": "$text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Undo carries the safety",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "y5ai98",
                      "name": "Body",
                      "fill": "$dim",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Promote exists to avoid losing work. Undo does that better: it restores the whole subtree, not just the children, and it covers the leaf case too. Soft delete is already in place, so this is a flag flip.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "aOIvH",
                  "name": "Confirm only when it earns it",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 5,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Tdz8v",
                      "name": "Title",
                      "fill": "$text",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Confirm only when it earns it",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 13,
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "XUeXc",
                      "name": "Body",
                      "fill": "$dim",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "A leaf deletes silently with an undo toast. A parent gets a dialog naming the count, because the consequence exceeds what the tap implied. Confirming everything trains people to dismiss dialogs unread.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
